publish	Build and publish both architectures	2026-10-21T06:57:43.1257656Z               "committer": {
publish	Build and publish both architectures	2026-10-21T06:57:43.1257873Z                 "email": "11675668+jerolan@users.noreply.github.com",
publish	Build and publish both architectures	2026-10-21T06:57:43.1258119Z                 "name": "Jerome Olvera"
publish	Build and publish both architectures	2026-10-21T06:57:43.1258307Z               },
publish	Build and publish both architectures	2026-10-21T06:57:43.1258494Z               "id": "efbb401f2a06a5881f0f189a3683836d62dcddc4",
publish	Build and publish both architectures	2026-10-21T06:57:43.1260034Z               "message": "Parse bounded ZIP debug archives\n\nSentry clients commonly upload dSYM bundles as ZIP archives. The server previously treated the archive itself as one unknown object, so every contained Mach-O or ELF remained unresolved.\n\nExpand ZIP uploads into independent debug objects within explicit entry and uncompressed-byte limits. Preserve each object name, symbols and CFI table, apply the parent Debug ID, and leave malformed or oversized archives non-fatal. Cover a bundle containing Mach-O and ELF through the authenticated HTTP Minidump path.",
